course: dictionary
lesson: 5264
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. The word journal is a good example. «Mia writes in her journal every night before bed.» Here a journal is a book where you write about your day, your thoughts and your feelings. It is a kind of diary.
explain: Now read this: «The article was published in a medical journal.» Here a journal is a serious magazine, where experts share their work on a subject such as medicine. The words article and published are the clues. They point to a magazine, not a diary.
explain: Always check the clues around the word, then try your meaning in the sentence. If «Mia writes in her magazine before bed» sounds wrong, then diary is the right meaning for that sentence.
fact: A journal is a book in which you write about what happens each day, your thoughts and your feelings. That is a kind of diary.
fact: A journal can also be a serious magazine about a subject, like science or medicine, where experts publish their work.
fact: In science, «published in a journal» means the work has been checked by other experts first.
fact: Journal can also mean a newspaper, as in «The Wall Street Journal». In bookkeeping, a journal is a record of money coming in and going out.
fact: «Writing worries in a diary, sometimes called journaling or a "brain dump", can help sort them out and calm the mind at bedtime.»
exercise: «Mia writes in her journal every night before bed.» What is a journal here? | A tin for keeping coins | *A book where you write about your day and your feelings | A kind of bus | A tall tree in the garden
exercise: Which word is the best clue that «a medical journal» is a magazine and not a diary? | The word results | The word medical sounds like medicine but is not a clue | The word was | *The word published
exercise: Elif says every journal is a diary. Is she right? | *No, a journal can also be a serious magazine for experts | No, journals are only for money | Yes, every journal is a diary | Yes, but only at bedtime
test: «Dad reads the journal with his morning coffee.» What does journal most likely mean in this sentence? | A diary of his thoughts | *A newspaper | A pot for coffee | A bus ticket
test: «The researchers sent their paper to a journal, and other experts checked it first.» What is a journal here? | A school bell | A book of jokes | A shop that sells chocolate | *A serious magazine where experts publish their work
exam: Kim says journal always means diary, but «The article was published in a medical journal» shows otherwise. What is the best explanation? | Journal only means money in bookkeeping | Journal is a word that is never used in sentences | *A journal can also be a serious magazine, and the word published is a clue | Kim is right, a journal is always a diary
